[Car Light Pair Thinning 25]
description=Car lights farther than 25 units: skips about half of the light pairs, always both lights of a pair. Closer cars keep every light. Sizes unchanged.
author=Generated from disassembly

// The car-light flare call at 0x19A454 goes to a stub at 0x28C148. The decision uses bit 21 of the lamp's car-local
// position x (the byte at +0x4E of the lamp object; the sign is not included), so mirrored left/right lights always
// get the same answer; centre-line lights are always kept. Only has an effect beyond the car cull distance if that is
// larger than this distance.
patch=1,EE,0028C148,word,8CC9000C
patch=1,EE,0028C14C,word,9129004E
patch=1,EE,0028C150,word,31290020
patch=1,EE,0028C154,word,8CC80008
patch=1,EE,0028C158,word,3C0BC1C8
patch=1,EE,0028C15C,word,0168502B
patch=1,EE,0028C160,word,000A480A
patch=1,EE,0028C164,word,3C190024
patch=1,EE,0028C168,word,37394990
patch=1,EE,0028C16C,word,03E9C80B
patch=1,EE,0028C170,word,03200008
patch=1,EE,0028C174,word,00000000
patch=1,EE,0019A454,word,0C0A3052

